<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Soninke</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Soninke are a Mande people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>, living in the area of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritania">Mauritania</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a>. They founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana-empire">Ghana Empire</a>, also known as Wagadou. Accounts of the Ghana Empire describe the Soninke as the empire's ruling people and traders.</p></div>
